  "title": "What Is Fabric IQ?! Microsoft Fabric\u2019s NEW Ontology Explained",
  "description": "\ud83d\udd25 Confused about Fabric IQ? You\u2019re not alone.\n\nWhen Fabric IQ was announced at Ignite, it looked powerful\u2026 but what does it actually DO?\n\nIn this video, we sit down with Devang Shah to break down what Fabric IQ really is inside Microsoft Fabric and why ontology might be the missing context layer your AI agents desperately need.\n\nYou\u2019ll learn:\n\n\u2714\ufe0f What Fabric IQ actually is\n\u2714\ufe0f What an ontology means in Microsoft Fabric\n\u2714\ufe0f How entity types and relationships work\n\u2714\ufe0f How to bind ontology to Lakehouse & Eventhouse\n\u2714\ufe0f Why AI agents need context (to avoid hallucinations!)\n\u2714\ufe0f How knowledge graphs improve reasoning\n\nFabric IQ allows you to:\n\nAdd meaning to your data\nCreate reusable AI context\nConnect transactional, analytical, and real-time data\nBuild a shared context layer for humans AND AI agents\n\n\u23f1\ufe0f Timeline\n00:00 \u2013 Intro\n00:27 \u2013 What is Fabric IQ?\n01:35 \u2013 Why ontology matters for AI\n02:01 \u2013 Retail ontology example walkthrough\n02:50 \u2013 Entity types & relationships explained\n03:40 \u2013 Binding ontology to Lakehouse\n04:10 \u2013 Real-time data with Eventhouse\n05:05 \u2013 Ontology overview & instances\n06:45 \u2013 3 reasons you should care about Fabric IQ\n07:45 \u2013 Should we do a \"how to\"?\n\n\ud83d\udc47 Should we bring Devang back for a full step-by-step setup tutorial? Let us know in the comments!\n\n\n*******************\n\nYooo! \ud83d\ude4c take your data skills to the next level and join fellow data professionals in our community THE CUBE: https://guyinacube.com\n\n\ud83c\udf10 LET'S CONNECT!\nOfficial website: https://guyinacube.com\nLinkedIn: \u00a0\u00a0/\u00a0guyinacube\u00a0\u00a0\nFacebook: \u00a0\u00a0/\u00a0guyinacube\u00a0\u00a0\nInstagram: \u00a0\u00a0/\u00a0guyinacube\u00a0\u00a0\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/guyinacube.com\nX: https://x.com/guyinacube\n\n\ud83c\udfa4 HOST\nMarthe Moengen\n\n#PowerBI #MCPServer #GitHubCopilot #ClaudeAI #GuyInACube",
